Thanks @DarkLight1337. I changed the follow-up so the batch request defaults for `temperature`, `top_p`, `min_p`, and `repetition_penalty` match `ChatCompletionRequest` (`None`), while explicit batch values are still preserved.

I also checked the no-defaults case: batch now falls back to normal chat's built-in `1.0 / 1.0 / 0.0 / 1.0` instead of the old batch-only `temperature=0.7`. The real `vllm serve` E2E still flips as expected:

```text
before direct {'temperature': 0.2, 'top_p': 0.5, 'min_p': 0.2, 'repetition_penalty': 1.3}
before batch  {'temperature': 0.7, 'top_p': 1.0, 'min_p': 0.0, 'repetition_penalty': 1.0}
after direct {'temperature': 0.2, 'top_p': 0.5, 'min_p': 0.2, 'repetition_penalty': 1.3}
after batch  {'temperature': 0.2, 'top_p': 0.5, 'min_p': 0.2, 'repetition_penalty': 1.3}
```

